The function below finds the first duplicate value in a list (the duplicate whose SECOND occurrence appears earliest), returning None if there are no duplicates. It has a bug that returns the wrong element in some cases because it does not preserve first-seen order. Fix it and return the complete corrected function.

def first_duplicate(nums):
    seen = set(nums)
    for n in seen:
        if nums.count(n) > 1:
            return n
    return None

